[{:db/id "q-355528/field-1/70e1944564d77e6c9f47ea90a958324b0fdca05ef3cf4a7aa3ae3b55bc80872a" :answer/id #uuid "abaa3130-f455-5f4c-bc41-d1d85b638552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x^2+3)^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186290355 :answer-field/choices ["q-355528/field-1/70e1944564d77e6c9f47ea90a958324b0fdca05ef3cf4a7aa3ae3b55bc80872a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355562/field-1/cbbd4cd1fd6ebf37e4d5854d9c5e4d0455bd954fa86bfb1294b548d531d05ca2" :answer/id #uuid "dfdc97e1-e0ec-505d-8873-6e496bf4b877" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{x^2/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355562/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "910d6a58-2678-5801-bc3d-52e3e8d75283" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355562/field-1/cbbd4cd1fd6ebf37e4d5854d9c5e4d0455bd954fa86bfb1294b548d531d05ca2" :answer-field/choices ["q-355562/field-1/cbbd4cd1fd6ebf37e4d5854d9c5e4d0455bd954fa86bfb1294b548d531d05ca2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355562" :question/id #uuid "86ea9e27-7410-5a64-bcd2-b11d02609395" :question/math-academy-id "q-355562" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=xy$  that satisfies $y(0)=1.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/2+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/2+C}\\, \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{{x}^{2}/2+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =K{e}^{0} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=xy$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{{x}^{2}/2}\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-355562/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355562"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-355578/field-1/3219d9327c0321782b72dcc33021d40b36ff4b0c77f4ee29bf47a19161f95698" :answer/id #uuid "5ec52982-94be-5d1f-baef-e86249afe96c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{2-1/x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355578/field-1/a638e74dd9a56876f6c763686f5098cf7667bd934e84804d6b352cd887aa4b9c" :answer/id #uuid "53a823d4-ace3-5415-83d3-0905a1781274" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{1-1/x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355578/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "786e4bda-f2b8-5dd2-b35d-3354a644b176" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355578/field-1/3219d9327c0321782b72dcc33021d40b36ff4b0c77f4ee29bf47a19161f95698" :answer-field/choices ["q-355578/field-1/3219d9327c0321782b72dcc33021d40b36ff4b0c77f4ee29bf47a19161f95698" "q-355578/field-1/a638e74dd9a56876f6c763686f5098cf7667bd934e84804d6b352cd887aa4b9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355578" :question/id #uuid "5ccd0d28-c2a6-553d-8006-d97ec4bdd759" :question/math-academy-id "q-355578" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}=0$  that satisfies $y(1)=e.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-1/x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-1/x+C}\\, \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-1/x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{-1/x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=e$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e & =K{e}^{-1} \\\\ K & ={e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}=0$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=e$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2-1/x}\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-355578/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355578"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-14312/selection/1ac12e33425986ab1ef357567a0cc7388186754ada8ecb053ef3e12f6ebad8e4" :answer/id #uuid "a20b712f-91dc-571d-9d75-f5df1c22a9f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-1+{e}^{-x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14312/selection/c6e19e65f1f84b01e5edc05289ab7af3804e394bbc234f644d9c00b4b4185a8e" :answer/id #uuid "5eaa1435-aec7-50ba-bc0b-1db151160857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{{e}^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14312/selection/0dcc3a052d1c2129957983132cf55797709600e6396210d655a1c27b40a17f87" :answer/id #uuid "b3f0397d-f762-54ab-bfdd-1867271964b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-{e}^{-x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14312/selection/b1ec571fe761ec621987daf580f2a7970faa815dc5b37fc27bccc7c8faa96535" :answer/id #uuid "60665b18-fb0e-5871-befd-870df448dc57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-1+x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14312/selection/8a4c600beab4c5fd7a4cad48dbe098520231d474467529db04153c011a9819c1" :answer/id #uuid "8af44e4c-6c1f-53ac-bc8c-919b300a5c71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-1-{e}^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14312/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "95c9a681-e457-5107-8106-bb2d53d5a093" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14312/selection/0dcc3a052d1c2129957983132cf55797709600e6396210d655a1c27b40a17f87" :answer-field/choices ["q-14312/selection/1ac12e33425986ab1ef357567a0cc7388186754ada8ecb053ef3e12f6ebad8e4" "q-14312/selection/c6e19e65f1f84b01e5edc05289ab7af3804e394bbc234f644d9c00b4b4185a8e" "q-14312/selection/0dcc3a052d1c2129957983132cf55797709600e6396210d655a1c27b40a17f87" "q-14312/selection/b1ec571fe761ec621987daf580f2a7970faa815dc5b37fc27bccc7c8faa96535" "q-14312/selection/8a4c600beab4c5fd7a4cad48dbe098520231d474467529db04153c011a9819c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14312" :question/id #uuid "a106a954-1ab0-5359-b8c4-675966fee9cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-14312" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{-x}$ that satisfies $y(0)={e}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,dx & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{e}^{-x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-{e}^{-x}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{e}^{-x}+C} \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{-{e}^{-x}+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{-{e}^{-x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)={e}^{-1}$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1} & =K{e}^{-{e}^{-0}} \\\\ {e}^{-1} & =K{e}^{-1} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{-x}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)={e}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-{e}^{-x}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-14312/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14312"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104065/selection/0a961ba0108a855819a887e3689f9fd641a03787a20f41170e46e5977bd76181" :answer/id #uuid "de00ee50-8fcd-56a0-80c9-ce55068425a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+8{x}^{2}-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104065/selection/ecebb567fe167c082d99fc84020fbb9cab56fa98086d9319dfd169e0c739b903" :answer/id #uuid "8106d8c2-18a0-547d-bee4-ccf27f8da73e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4{x}^{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104065/selection/215a97036edd4c3e737f4af134d973333b22c036fbd36ab9010dfb0dedf20d70" :answer/id #uuid "8a8a68c0-e78f-5b95-9b4d-daac33153ffb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8{x}^{2}-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104065/selection/aa0249ca86c86a7a3d3335697022b5d749f95b7d00a2d7d6e373e0a320927fa6" :answer/id #uuid "b5c4af94-99f3-5b11-a092-e4831c2dad7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104065/selection/4ee75af43bdf25398c28e55aa892878898ea7db8d852176f7a8286686adad178" :answer/id #uuid "033fdcc9-58c7-5818-908c-7a1b4029fcf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104065/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c26e6cf-2d22-5091-8bf9-ee65799df215" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104065/selection/aa0249ca86c86a7a3d3335697022b5d749f95b7d00a2d7d6e373e0a320927fa6" :answer-field/choices ["q-104065/selection/0a961ba0108a855819a887e3689f9fd641a03787a20f41170e46e5977bd76181" "q-104065/selection/ecebb567fe167c082d99fc84020fbb9cab56fa98086d9319dfd169e0c739b903" "q-104065/selection/215a97036edd4c3e737f4af134d973333b22c036fbd36ab9010dfb0dedf20d70" "q-104065/selection/aa0249ca86c86a7a3d3335697022b5d749f95b7d00a2d7d6e373e0a320927fa6" "q-104065/selection/4ee75af43bdf25398c28e55aa892878898ea7db8d852176f7a8286686adad178"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104065" :question/id #uuid "e80102fb-b0d5-5bdb-8b2c-e58b30c1b434" :question/math-academy-id "q-104065" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ that satisfies $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}.$ Assume that $0<x<\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+8x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x+8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x+4{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the right-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nwhere $C={C}_{1}+{C}_{2}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})+4{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+C & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡1+{\\pi }^{2}+C & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ that satisfies the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104065/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104065"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79373/selection/94182831d2d63d628b5e4a0fd4caccdf43bae40baa7c405857dffdcfd3d3ef85" :answer/id #uuid "5155c528-33b5-51dd-84fa-cafed472a4e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79373/selection/a0505c2a547a8a2a586916286410f92f8f61bf5688eec10075f26326dfd1b547" :answer/id #uuid "fa790788-a417-5e4e-b69f-a99f474a6e7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79373/selection/ccd62cbb1c79fcc2b7f87defe7c08c578fb5c4292434b44ce8a3499e3bf9b9ea" :answer/id #uuid "c60ed70a-2599-5383-95f7-650d0857f471" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{4}-x+2}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79373/selection/fdb1d99be788cd30c0b9628e6d2c335181576a5da2edb923b90df88734f20c44" :answer/id #uuid "79d1a842-07f7-57e7-b42c-950fee6afbcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79373/selection/72044ac3bb0971bb979307a24116fa63413c49c0e19390e6d975535cd54e3544" :answer/id #uuid "0b23911a-877a-5e80-8175-132810929a84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2x-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79373/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "271a6a6e-af64-539e-b578-ddb2b11702e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79373/selection/fdb1d99be788cd30c0b9628e6d2c335181576a5da2edb923b90df88734f20c44" :answer-field/choices ["q-79373/selection/94182831d2d63d628b5e4a0fd4caccdf43bae40baa7c405857dffdcfd3d3ef85" "q-79373/selection/a0505c2a547a8a2a586916286410f92f8f61bf5688eec10075f26326dfd1b547" "q-79373/selection/ccd62cbb1c79fcc2b7f87defe7c08c578fb5c4292434b44ce8a3499e3bf9b9ea" "q-79373/selection/fdb1d99be788cd30c0b9628e6d2c335181576a5da2edb923b90df88734f20c44" "q-79373/selection/72044ac3bb0971bb979307a24116fa63413c49c0e19390e6d975535cd54e3544"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79373" :question/id #uuid "f5584487-f86c-5569-83ea-05d79037610f" :question/math-academy-id "q-79373" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y} & =4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}-{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(4{x}^{3}-1){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}-1 \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (4{x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{4}-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{4}-1+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡C & =0 \\\\ C & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79373/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79373"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
